  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved labour administration system to ensure effective labour law compliance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support from the ILO for the functioning of the Tripartite Social Partnership Commission (TSPC) has led to gradual improvement over time, however, institutional challenges remain. A key priority is strengthening the TSPC by improving its strategic planning, institutional capacity, and stakeholder engagement. Efforts include developing the 2025&#x2013;2026 Strategic Plan, revitalizing social dialogue at national and regional levels, and exploring a tripartite &#x201c;social contract&#x201d; to align economic and labour market goals. 
Collective bargaining is not used widely in Georgia. While Georgia&#x2019;s regulatory framework has been reinforced in recent years, it leaves out many areas in which employers and trade unions might engage in collective bargaining. To enhance collective bargaining, the ILO supports the development of a legal gap analysis and case studies on bargaining incentives. 
Individual labour disputes in Georgia need to be resolved through the judicial system, where a backlog of cases means it often takes years before a case is considered in the final instance. This leads to a lack of protection of worker rights and a loss of productivity. The ILO supports an analysis of challenges in individual dispute resolution and support reforms to streamline processes and ensure faster, more effective case resolution. 
In the area of wages, the ILO supports the establishment of a tripartite minimum wage policy board, ensuring wage adjustments are evidence-based and aligned with international standards, including ILO Convention No. 131. Capacity building for national statistical authorities will strengthen data collection and monitoring to inform policy decisions. 
Finally, occupational safety and health (OSH) remains a priority, with continued support to the Labour Inspection Office. This includes legal and policy reviews, training programs, and awareness-raising campaigns to embed a strong OSH culture across workplaces.</narrative>
  </description>
